From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Wed, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: recore: enable CONFIG_CMD_BMP so the splash screen can work

recore_defconfig already sets CONFIG_SPLASH_SCREEN, CONFIG_BMP_*BPP and
CONFIG_VIDEO_BMP_RLE8, and a boot.bmp is shipped - but none of it does
anything, because splash_display() is only ever called from
common/stdio.c under:

	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPLASH_SCREEN) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CMD_BMP))
		splash_display();

Without CMD_BMP that call is compiled out entirely, so the whole splash
configuration is inert. (What is on screen today is CONFIG_VIDEO_LOGO,
U-Boot's own built-in logo, which is a different mechanism.)

This only enables the capability. Displaying boot.bmp still needs the
image loaded and shown, e.g. from the boot script:

	load ${devtype} ${devnum} ${loadaddr} ${prefix}boot.bmp
	bmp display ${loadaddr}

CONFIG_SPLASH_SOURCE is deliberately not enabled: sunxi defines no
splash_locations[], so it has nowhere to load from on this platform.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 configs/recore_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/recore_defconfig b/configs/recore_defconfig
--- a/configs/recore_defconfig
+++ b/configs/recore_defconfig
@@ -32,3 +32,4 @@
 CONFIG_CMD_REGULATOR=y
 CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
 CONFIG_PREBOOT="mw.l 0x01f01400 0x00020102; usb reset; run bootcmd_usb0"
+CONFIG_CMD_BMP=y
